1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,264
When you're walking around one place you definitely will find is the area of gambler star aka the old town.
漫步时一定会走到老城一带；地名在原字幕中疑似误识别。

2
00:00:07,264 --> 00:00:11,951
You'll notice that the streets and buildings are incredibly old.
你会注意到街道和建筑都非常古老。

3
00:00:11,951 --> 00:00:18,703
You'll find cobbled streets literally everywhere and it's a fun place to explore even if you don't know where you're going.
鹅卵石街道到处都是，即使不知道要去哪里，也很值得随意探索。

4
00:00:18,703 --> 00:00:22,860
You'll eventually find your way into the main town square.
你最终会走到老城的主广场。

5
00:00:23,640 --> 00:00:29,700
This is and is possibly the most photographed area in all of stockholm.
这里可能是斯德哥尔摩被拍照最多的地方；原字幕此处有不完整指称。

6
00:00:29,700 --> 00:00:34,740
There's no shortage of things to photograph or places to eat around here.
这里不缺可拍的景物，也不缺吃饭的地方。

7
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:41,481
If you're taking one of the many walking tours available they usually start right here into the torreyet.
如果参加步行导览，许多团会从这儿出发；广场专名待听辨。

8
00:00:41,481 --> 00:00:46,334
The main attraction you'll find here is the nobel prize museum.
这里主要的参观点是诺贝尔奖博物馆。

9
00:00:46,334 --> 00:00:54,780
Now if you don't know anything about alfred nobel or what prices go in what categories you can easily learn it here.
不了解阿尔弗雷德·诺贝尔或奖项分类的话，可以在这里了解。

10
00:00:55,560 --> 00:01:02,273
And the museum itself is a very interesting look at some of the innovations that have changed the world for the better.
博物馆也呈现了一些让世界变得更好的创新。

11
00:01:02,273 --> 00:01:05,884
You'll recognize some of the names of the nobel prize winners.
有些诺贝尔奖得主的名字你会认得。

12
00:01:05,884 --> 00:01:11,460
And some of them you might never have heard of but you can look up every single one of them from here.
有些可能没听过，但都能在这里查到。

13
00:01:12,720 --> 00:01:19,953
Whilst you're walking around gamlastan you'll fall in love with the picturesque streets the amazing views across the water.
漫步老城，你会爱上如画街道和对岸的美景。

14
00:01:19,953 --> 00:01:23,940
And chilling out in one of the many eateries that's on the waterfront.
也能在众多水岸餐馆里坐下来休息。

15
00:01:24,600 --> 00:01:29,820
If you get a chance to eat mr french here you'll be treated like royalty.
作者说有机会去 Mr French 吃饭，会受到贵宾般的招待。

16
00:01:29,820 --> 00:01:34,500
Speaking of food there is a tradition here in Sweden called fica.
说到吃，作者介绍瑞典有一种叫 fika 的传统；字幕拼写待复核。

17
00:01:34,500 --> 00:01:38,085
This is effectively socializing over coffee and baked goods.
他的解释是，边喝咖啡、吃烘焙点心，边和人交流。

18
00:01:38,085 --> 00:01:45,713
And there's no shortage of places around the city where you can buy reasonably priced coffee and cakes and sit around and socialize.
城里很多地方可以买到价格合理的咖啡、蛋糕，坐下来聊聊天。

19
00:01:45,713 --> 00:01:50,245
Even if you have to make do with 7 eleven coffee and donuts.
即使只能用便利店的咖啡和甜甜圈将就一下。

20
00:01:50,245 --> 00:01:54,480
It's always nice to enjoy a coffee break somewhere here in stockholm.
在斯德哥尔摩找个地方喝杯咖啡休息，总是不错。

21
00:01:55,680 --> 00:02:00,360
If you look across the water you'll see a small island known as rita holman.
望向水对岸，会看到作者所说的一座小岛；地名原字幕待核。

22
00:02:00,360 --> 00:02:09,656
There's not much to it it's got some iconic buildings and a nice square but the main attraction is this read a hoban church.
那里有标志性建筑和漂亮广场，主要看点是一座教堂。

23
00:02:09,656 --> 00:02:18,771
Unlike stockholm cathedral which celebrates births and weddings rita holman church is used if a member of the swedish royal family dies.
作者将其与举行出生、婚礼仪式的大教堂比较，说这座教堂用于王室丧葬。

24
00:02:18,771 --> 00:02:28,620
The best way to describe this place is that it's an incredibly fancy graveyard as this is the final resting place for most of sweden's iconic royals.
他形容这像座十分华丽的墓园，许多瑞典王室成员安葬于此。

25
00:02:29,520 --> 00:02:33,372
It's pretty kooky to see quite a lot of them on display.
看到这么多王室成员的相关陈列，作者觉得有点奇异。

26
00:02:33,372 --> 00:02:38,751
What's also on display are the plaques of the former royals from around the world that have died.
还展有来自世界各地、已故王室成员的纪念牌。

27
00:02:38,751 --> 00:02:45,006
So the plaques that you saw before at the royal palace once a royal dies they end up here.
先前王宫看到的那些牌子，按作者说法，在相关王室成员去世后会移来这里。

28
00:02:45,006 --> 00:02:47,615
And this one makes me particularly sad.
这一块让他尤其难过。

29
00:02:47,615 --> 00:02:53,148
The plaque of our beloved queen elizabeth ii rip mom we miss you daily.
他指着伊丽莎白二世的纪念牌致意，说他们每天都怀念她；字幕末尾称呼待听辨。

30
00:02:53,148 --> 00:02:59,160
But a visit to rita holman church is definitely worth it mainly for the history and nostalgia.
作者仍觉得很值得来，主要为了这里的历史感与怀旧情绪。

31
00:02:59,160 --> 00:03:07,080
And if you can get over the fact that you're literally surrounded by hundreds of dead bodies the church itself is actually quite nice.
如果能接受周围安葬着许多逝者这件事，教堂本身其实很漂亮。

32
00:03:07,080 --> 00:03:13,062
It's very soothing and calming it's very quiet and you'll actually have a good time.
环境很舒缓、很安静，作者觉得参观体验会不错。

33
00:03:13,062 --> 00:03:18,420
I know that sounds weird given that you're in a giant mausoleum but yeah definitely worth checking out.
他说，在大陵墓里这样评价可能听着奇怪，但确实值得参观。
